; The one way an opaque slot adds a diagnostic.
;
; `(anchor :name origin)` is a perfectly good declaration, and it sits
; inside a `:body`. Every descent stops at an opaque slot, the cross-ref
; index pass included, so `origin` is never registered and the
; reference below finds an empty registry:
;
;   not_cross_ref at [apply target]
;   form `apply` keyword `:target` expects `anchor-name`, got `origin`
;   (no `(template/anchor :name …)` form declares this name)
;
; The repair is not at the reference. Move the anchor out of the body
; (one line up, to the top level) and it registers as it always did.
; The alternative repair, declaring the slot readable, is a schema
; change and not the author's to make.
;
;   cat examples/plugins/opaque-slot/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/opaque-slot/example-hidden-target.sjon | sjon validate - --no-project

(template :name intro
  :body (anchor :name origin))

(apply :template intro :target origin)
